{#-
  Tells an operator that somebody has sent feedback. It says who, what it
  is about and where it was sent from, and links to it.

  Never the message. Somebody describing a fault pastes what they were
  looking at, so the message may hold patient data, and an email would
  copy it into a system outside Quill. It stays behind the application's
  own access checks, one press away. Context:
    sender    the username of whoever sent it
    category  what they said it was about, in words, or None
    route     the page it was sent from, as a route pattern, or ""
    url       the link to the feedback in the admin area
-#}
{% extends "base.html.j2" %}
{% import "_components.html.j2" as c with context %}
{% block subject %}New feedback from {{ sender }}{% endblock %}
{% block preheader %}
{%- if category %}{{ category }}.{% else %}Open it in Quill to read it.{% endif -%}
{% endblock %}
{% block body %}
{{ c.heading("New *feedback*") }}
{{ c.paragraph(sender ~ " has sent feedback through Quill.") }}
{% if category %}{{ c.paragraph("About: " ~ category) }}{% endif %}
{% if route %}{{ c.paragraph("Sent from: " ~ route) }}{% endif %}
{{ c.button("Read the feedback", url) }}
{{ c.small("The message is not in this email. It may hold patient details, so it stays in Quill.") }}
{% endblock %}
{% block reason %}You are receiving this because this address is set to be told of new feedback on Quill.{% endblock %}
{% block text %}
{{ sender }} has sent feedback through Quill.
{% if category %}
About: {{ category }}
{% endif %}
{% if route %}
Sent from: {{ route }}
{% endif %}

Read the feedback: {{ url }}

The message is not in this email. It may hold patient details, so it stays in Quill.
{% endblock %}
